# High-volume local benchmark telemetry.
# direct-saturation-<rate>.json holds full per-repeat sample series,
# injector-<rate>-<repeat>.json holds full per-event injector output,
# postgres-diagnostics-raw-<label>.json holds full per-tick pg_stat_activity/
# pg_locks sample series, and cpu-scheduling-raw-<label>.json holds full
# per-tick cgroup/proc/PSI/probe sample series - from
# scripts/benchmark/direct_saturation.py, direct_injector.py,
# postgres_diagnostics.py, and cpu_scheduling_diagnostics.py respectively.
# All are useful locally for analysis but make commits/history
# unnecessarily large. Compact evidence (README rows,
# postgres-diagnostics-summary-*.json, cpu-scheduling-summary-*.json,
# EXPLAIN output, migration artifacts) stays tracked - only these raw
# telemetry filenames are excluded.
artifacts/benchmark/**/direct-saturation.json
artifacts/benchmark/**/direct-saturation-*.json
artifacts/benchmark/**/injector-*.json
artifacts/benchmark/**/postgres-diagnostics-raw-*.json
artifacts/benchmark/**/cpu-scheduling-raw-*.json
